(7499926, 1194093, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Senthil!  This is a lovely shot and did very well in a very tough challenge, so you should be proud of it.  The choice of setting and time of day are just perfect, the colours and tones harmonious and peaceful, and the towers and their reflections add a sense of the exotic to the shot.  Love the leading lines and sense of place you have created.<br/> <br/>In terms of nitpicks...honestly I am having a hard time finding any flaws. OK here''s one, the horizon is just too much at the exact middle of the pic; either a third higher or lower could have won you a ribbon.  Your settings are bang on for the subject.<br/> <br/>Hope this critique has been of help.  Feel free to pm me with any questions.  And in the meantime please continue to shoot and enter, sometimes it takes awhile for us to get through all the requested critiques.  Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Senthil!  This is a lovely shot and did very well in a very tough challenge, so you should be proud of it.  The choice of setting and time of day are just perfect, the colours and tones harmonious and peaceful, and the towers and their reflections add a sense of the exotic to the shot.  Love the leading lines and sense of place you have created. In terms of nitpicks...honestly I am having a hard time finding any flaws. OK here''s one, the horizon is just too much at the exact middle of the pic; either a third higher or lower could have won you a ribbon.  Your settings are bang on for the subject. Hope this critique has been of help.  Feel free to pm me with any questions.  And in the meantime please continue to shoot and enter, sometimes it takes awhile for us to get through all the requested critiques.  Susan', '2017-02-15 20:54:27.000000', NULL, 0),
